			title: "Antimatter Trap"
			x: 9.5d
			y: 9.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["16D1550DF465D570"]
			description: ["The &6Fibre Draw Tower&r pulls a preform of ytterbium-doped glass into optical fibre, and writes the grating that makes it a laser. MCVD makes the preform in three operations: soot deposited inside a fused silica tube, solution doping with ytterbium, then drying, sintering and collapse. Ultraviolet light writes the Bragg grating. Its controller, clean room casing, PTFE pipe and a heatproof draw furnace; fused silica tubes, silicon tetrachloride and ytterbium chloride solution. The fibre laser modules for the fusion chamber and the sail launcher. Chlorine from the soot goes to the network and the glass dust goes back in; keep both sealed and stock the fibre by ME."]
			icon: "gtceu:fibre_draw_tower"
			id: "33CBE187D3DF4EA8"
			rewards: [{ id: "340D8B303B909940", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "7052083D5408A302", item: "gtceu:fibre_draw_tower", type: "item" }
				{ id: "31651AA9F4CA8612", item: "gtceu:clean_machine_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "14AC5C80C47EDC4F", item: "grindless:fused_silica_tube", type: "item" }
				{ id: "54746962ECF70862", item: "grindless:mcvd_soot_tube", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1C9A67AF121FE5AE", item: "grindless:doped_soot_tube", type: "item" }
				{ id: "7BA69F1A79F4E451", item: "grindless:yb_doped_preform", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Fibre Draw Tower"
			x: 5.0d
			y: 11.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["33CBE187D3DF4EA8"]
			description: ["A length of fibre with a Bragg grating at each end is a laser. The &6Fibre Laser Module&r is what the big chambers fire."]
			icon: "grindless:fibre_laser_module"
			id: "51F3CB52EBEB3BCB"
			rewards: [{ id: "56B4C30A70CF7509", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "1EA6CADF664FD09D", item: "grindless:fibre_laser_module", type: "item" }]
			title: "Fibre Laser Module"
			x: 8.0d
			y: 11.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["51F3CB52EBEB3BCB"]
			description: ["The &6MOCVD Reactor&r grows compound semiconductors one atomic layer at a time. It makes the organometallics, grows indium gallium arsenide, cleaves diode bars (eight per wafer), coats the facets with alumina and titania mirrors, and mounts four bars on copper as a pump module. A niobium nitride film is its other job. Its controller, clean room casing, an inert casing for the gas cabinet and a filter hood; gallium, gallium arsenide wafers and arsine. InGaAs pump modules, which light the fibre, and the SNSPD film. Arsenic is contained: the arsine by-product goes to the scrubber as arsenic and hydrogen. Keep the scrubber supplied and the modules going out by ME."]
			icon: "gtceu:mocvd_reactor"
			id: "3D71CDF674EF3302"
			rewards: [{ id: "71C9A097B98E6CC3", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "33CC90ED047DEB79", item: "gtceu:mocvd_reactor", type: "item" }
				{ id: "323B70DCDE4C50F9", item: "gtceu:clean_machine_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "364A7A6804C28042", item: "gtceu:inert_machine_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "308996C0B3D139EB", item: "grindless:ingaas_diode_bar", type: "item" }
				{ id: "3CDDC9D4118318EC", item: "grindless:coated_diode_bar", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "MOCVD Reactor"
			x: 10.5d
			y: 11.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3D71CDF674EF3302"]
			description: ["Diode bars stacked in a cooled mount make the &6InGaAs Pump Module&r that lights the fibre laser. The diode line builds it from InGaAs bars and a cooled mount, so it needs the pump line running. It unlocks the fibre laser and what that laser powers. Diodes go out by ME, a few at a time."]
			icon: "grindless:ingaas_pump_module"
			id: "346C198E81F5FA85"
			rewards: [{ id: "15A975F189427D96", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			tasks: [{ id: "70951C01EEF6B329", item: "grindless:ingaas_pump_module", type: "item" }]
			title: "Pump Diode Module"
			x: 12.25d
			y: 10.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["16D1550DF465D570"]
			description: ["The &6Zone Refining Tower&r sweeps germanium's impurities to the ends of a bar, over and over, until it is purer than almost anything you make. Its controller and clean room casing; eight RF coils ring the tower. The HPGe crystal, further along. Germanium bars in and crystals out by ME; the tower runs for a long time per bar."]
			icon: "gtceu:zone_refining_tower"
			id: "1ADBEF1F47053EC9"
			rewards: [{ id: "1C883F1697D2369F", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "7C0F424069AE78EE", item: "gtceu:zone_refining_tower", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1BCE898F913010CB", item: "gtceu:clean_machine_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Zone Refining Tower"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 13.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1ADBEF1F47053EC9"]
			description: ["The &6Optical Ground Station&r is the only reader of the Starshot: a primary mirror, adaptive optics and a photon counter. Its controller, UV casing, aluminium mirror blocks, computer casings for the optics bench and an SNSPD array. The Proxima approach data. Nothing to automate: it waits for the probe. Keep it powered and chunk-loaded."]
			icon: "gtceu:optical_ground_station"
			id: "5D40D7F4F07C52B6"
			rewards: [{ id: "36C021FC939B4DE5", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "3DE63636D2508532", item: "gtceu:optical_ground_station", type: "item" }
				{ id: "3CD446B1EABD8A5F", item: "gtceu:uv_machine_casing", type: "item" }
				{ id: "34A4B8D9300D4855", item: "gtceu:computer_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Optical Ground Station"
			x: 5.5d
			y: 13.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["16D1550DF465D570"]
			description: ["The &6Boron Nitride Reactor&r grows hexagonal BN and boron nitride nanotubes, a fibre stronger than carbon that shrugs off neutrons. Its controller, UV casing, naquadah coils and a PTFE pipe run. BNNT yarn for the tank and the probe frames. Boron-10 comes from the hot cell; send the yarn on by ME."]
			icon: "gtceu:boron_nitride_reactor"
			id: "37B93B08FCFF08DA"
			rewards: [{ id: "5AE77E610961C458", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "724959B8E5DCC24F", item: "gtceu:boron_nitride_reactor", type: "item" }
				{ id: "1A5A4DC542D26628", item: "gtceu:uv_machine_casing", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Boron Nitride Reactor"
			x: 7.0d
			y: 13.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["37B93B08FCFF08DA"]
			description: ["Spin the tubes and you get &6BNNT Yarn&r: light, strong and transparent to neutrons, so it is the fibre of the lightest parts. The yarn spinner makes it from boron nitride nanotubes, which need boron-10 from the hot cell. It unlocks the powder-in-tube line. Keep the tubes coming by ME and send the yarn on the same way."]
			icon: "grindless:bnnt_yarn"
			id: "3E5A326AEACCF50A"
			rewards: [{ id: "5B77C236091ED375", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			tasks: [
				{ id: "3FF00B5E97DCDCFF", item: "grindless:bnnt_yarn", type: "item" }
				{ id: "115D1CE589407BD8", item: "grindless:hbn_dust", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "BNNT Yarn"
			x: 8.75d
			y: 13.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["3E5A326AEACCF50A"]
			description: ["The &6Powder-in-Tube Line&r packs a wire powder into a silver sheath and draws it down, turning one ingot of material into four. Its controller and UV casing, a drawing bench and a furnace coil. EnTED wire for the UV network. Each billet eats one silver tube; the wire step returns silver dust. Remelt it into tubes and keep them stocked."]
			icon: "gtceu:powder_in_tube_line"
			id: "1682DED202B72CC5"
			rewards: [{ id: "7C90A2D8E0B2EC85", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [
